00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:06.710 align:start position:0%
eu agriculture ministers will exchange  views in luxembourg  on a report on the functioning of the  fruit and vegetable sector  since reforms were introduced in 2007.  the report concerns the implementation  of provisions on producer organizations  operational funds and operational  programs  the 2007 reform aim to strengthen the  role of fruit and vegetable producer  organizations  it provides a wider range of tools to  help prevent and manage  market crises incentives were created to  encourage  mergers between producer organizations  and associations  and to foster transnational cooperation  however the report points out that  there's little or no organization in the  fruit and vegetable sector in some eu  regions  this rules out benefits of specific aid  for seen for the sector  it also weakens the bargaining power of  producers within the supply chain  based on results from the minister's  debate the european commission could  later present the legislative proposals  to revise the eu  aid scheme for the fruit and vegetable  sector
 

